{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1225937-dawn-on-the-isle-help-creating-balancing-evocations","id":1225937,"title":"Dawn on the Isle: Help creating/balancing Evocations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-08T11:33:21-07:00","id":1225937,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Dawn on the Isle: Help creating/balancing Evocations","content":"Running my first 3e Exalted game, and was looking for help with evocations. Not sure how to balance them, what costs to give them, or how far into a tree you need to get before weird stuff starts happening. <br /> Anywhoozles, quick rundown of the artifacts and themes in question.<br /> <br /> <b>Patient Avalanche</b> (White Jade Powerbow) themes of patience/aiming and natural disasters) no evocations yet<br /> <br /> <b>Berserker Claws</b> (Red Jade/Soulsteel Razor Claws) I think the player's name choice for this one is a little flat, could use some zhooshing up, the player wanted the berserk animal trait? not sure if thats a good idea as it basically is what the Battle Fury Focus Charm does. Any way it could synergize with that well? Intended to use with Tiger style.<br /> <br /> <b>Confessor </b>(Blue Jade/Orichalcum Longfang) another working title, maybe something like Calumny? unearthing the secrets and emotional baggage of others?<br /> <br /> <b>Every Prick </b>(Green Jade/Starmetal Throwing Needle) just gave this player the first evocation from Spring Razor for now. Was also thinking of something like being able to make an attack in an empty room, sticking the needle into the wall or chair or somesuch, and when the target eventually enters the inadvertently prick themselves, and the needle returns to the assassin informing them of the hit. This feels super flavorful, but i have no idea how to crunch it, or how powerful/too powerful it could be, or how far down an evocation tree to put that.<br /> <br /> and lastly<br /> <b>Fox Tears </b>(Black Jade/Moonsilver Flute) the player is a Nightingale martial artist, so wanted a weapon/instrument. and is the only player to write an evocation of their own.<br /> <br /> Tears of Another<br /> 13m<br /> Duration -one scene<br /> Performace +Cha +known target intimacy, to share emotions of the target with all listeners. Those who hear must spend WP and resist Wits+Integrity or be unable attack or otherwise stop the performer from performing.<br /> <br /> Not sure what i think about this one. Doesn't actually seem like an evocation?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, any and all help is greatly appreciated =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24102-tweedbarista","name":"Tweedbarista","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T12:33:23-07:00","id":1225949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tweedbarista</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1225937-dawn-on-the-isle-help-creating-balancing-evocations#post1225937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Every Prick </b>(Green Jade/Starmetal Throwing Needle) just gave this player the first evocation from Spring Razor for now. Was also thinking of something like being able to make an attack in an empty room, sticking the needle into the wall or chair or somesuch, and when the target eventually enters the inadvertently prick themselves, and the needle returns to the assassin informing them of the hit. This feels super flavorful, but i have no idea how to crunch it, or how powerful/too powerful it could be, or how far down an evocation tree to put that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems fine to me - needles have the Subtle tag, meaning they can't inflict damage, just deliver poisons. The ability to ambush your target from afar to deliver some kind of poison <i>if </i>you're willing to cope with not having your weapon with you in the meantime and willing to deal with the risk of infiltration and the chance that your opponent will just... avoid the place you've left your thing for a longer time than you expected doesn't exactly seem terribly broken to me as long as you put some reasonable limiting factor on the Evocation (like a WP cost) to avoid a situation where the character is walking from room to room in her opponent's estate, sticking it in the wall and making some noise to lure her target there until he's loaded up with five different kinds of poison. You probably also want to give a detection difficulty to the needle (or maybe a rolloff against the character's conceal evidence result).<br /> <br /> In fact, I think this can easily be the very first evocation of your artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T12:40:26-07:00","id":1225952,"title":"","content":"Patient Avalanche and Confessor both sound cool. Can't really comment on balance without more specifics. The only thing that looks especially hard to balance would be if Patient Avalanche can push enemies/create difficult terrain/knock prone/otherwise keep enemies at a distance, and/or if it can speed up aiming. For Confessor, I'd borrow+modify charms from Calumny or other social artifact weapons.<br /> Berserker Claws: Does your player have Battle Fury Focus? If they don't, overlap with BFF doesn't sound like a large problem. Reversing wound penalties is probably something that should require a simple action to turn on. One way to synergies with BFF is effects that grant bonuses from having wound penalties but don't cancel the wound penalties (bonus dice to damage, charms only useable at certain wound penalties, etc), and leave cancelling them to Battle Fury Focus/Bloodthirsty Sword Dancer Spirit. Possibly effects that cost health levels, to get wound penalties for other effects to use/cancel?<br /> Every Prick's ability sounds like it might be sort of similar to White Veil style's ways to make non-damaging decisive attacks that don't put you at much risk. Given that that's an essence 1 charm with no prerequisites I agree that it could be early.<br /> Tears of Another seems a lot like Respect-Commanding attitude, so I would probably balance against that. Would the wits+integrity roll have a difficulty of the initial performance check, or something else? I think that performance tends to have better dice tricks than integrity, so that could end up a very difficulty check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}